A2UI stands for Agent-to-User Interface. It is an open-source, declarative protocol introduced by Google that allows AI agents to generate rich, interactive user interfaces rather than just plain text. Think of it as a “universal language” for UI. Instead of an AI agent trying to write complex code (like HTML or JavaScript) that might be buggy or insecure, it sends a simple JSON blueprint of what the interface should look like. Your app then takes that blueprint and builds it using its own “native” buttons and forms.

